From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 15:57:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] arm64: dts: exynos7870: add the cluster clocks to cpu0
 and cpu4

Wire the cluster clocks into the CPU nodes, as on Exynos850: cpu0 gets
cluster0_clk from cmu_cpucl0 and cpu4 gets cluster1_clk from
cmu_cpucl1. They are the policy CPUs of the two clusters, and
cpufreq-dt uses the clock of the policy CPU.

The supplies and the operating point tables are board specific and are
left to the board device tree.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
---

Notes:
    Origin: https://github.com/alessandro-fontana/linux-exynos7870 commit 98416dcfc0e4 (branch gtaxlwifi/7.3). Port to v7.3.4: applied unchanged (git am, no fuzz).

 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870.dtsi | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870.dtsi
index 0f662e5..859db6b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870.dtsi
@@ -74,6 +74,8 @@
 			compatible = "arm,cortex-a53";
 			reg = <0x0>;
 			enable-method = "psci";
+			clocks = <&cmu_cpucl0 CLK_CLUSTER0_SCLK>;
+			clock-names = "cluster0_clk";
 		};
 
 		cpu1: cpu@1 {
@@ -102,6 +104,8 @@
 			compatible = "arm,cortex-a53";
 			reg = <0x100>;
 			enable-method = "psci";
+			clocks = <&cmu_cpucl1 CLK_CLUSTER1_SCLK>;
+			clock-names = "cluster1_clk";
 		};
 
 		cpu5: cpu@101 {
